<section>
  <section>
    <h1>Accessibility testing with a screenreader</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>A screenreader</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Speaks what's on the screen with a synthetic voice</li>
      <li>Optionally controls a braille display</li>
      <li>Provides as much semantic/meta information as available</li>
      <li>Helps the user navigate</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>A screenreader user</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not use a mouse; only keyboard shortcuts</li>
      <li>Has no overview over the screen</li>
      <li>
        Goes through the screen in a certain order without knowing what will
        come later
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to use?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Many additional keyboard shortcuts</li>
      <li>Different paradigm to navigate the screen</li>
      <li>Interaction modes</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.smashingmagazine.com/2015/03/web-accessibility-with-accessibility-api/">
          How do screenreaders get their information?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://tink.uk/understanding-screen-reader-interaction-modes/">
          Understanding screen reader interaction modes
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Examples</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>MacOs: VoiceOver</li>
      <li>Windows: JAWS, NVDA</li>
      <li>IOS: VoiceOver</li>
      <li>Android: Talkback</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>VoiceOver</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Built into MacOs</li>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.apple.com/accessibility/mac/vision/">
          Apple info page
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a target="tweede" href="https://webaim.org/articles/voiceover/">
          Using VoiceOver to Evaluate Web Accessibility
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Non Visual Desktop Access</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Open source screenreader for Windows:{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.nvaccess.org/">
          download NVDA
        </a>{' '}
        and please make a donation
      </li>
      <li>Install or create portable version</li>
      <li>
        Default voice is rather robotic;{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://vocalizer-nvda.com/">
          buy better ones
        </a>
      </li>

      <li>
        <a target="tweede" href="https://webaim.org/articles/nvda/">
          Using NVDA to Evaluate Web Accessibility
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Job Access With Speech</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Commercial screenreader for Windows:{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="http://www.freedomscientific.com/Downloads/JAWS">
          download JAWS
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>40 minute trial version</li>
      <li>Many users don't have most recent version</li>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="http://www.freedomscientific.com/training/Surfs-Up/_Surfs_Up_Start_Here.htm">
          Tutorial: Surfing the Internet with JAWS
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a target="tweede" href="https://webaim.org/articles/jaws/">
          Using JAWS to Evaluate Web Accessibility
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Best supported combinations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>JAWS + Chrome or Edge</li>
      <li>NVDA + Chrome</li>
      <li>VoiceOver + Safari</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Setup</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unplug mouse, turn track pad off</li>
      <li>Turn off or cover your screen</li>
      <li>Use head phones</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>NVDA welcome screen</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Select your keyboard layout</li>
      <li>If your laptop has no INS key, then set Capslock as NVDA Key</li>
      <li>Uncheck "show this dialog when NVDA starts"</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Speech viewer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To read on the screen what NVDA says</li>
      <li>NVDA+N -> Tools -> Speech viewer</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>User guide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Open the user guide and keyboard shortcuts via NVDA+N -> Help</li>
      <li>Available in many languages</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Screen layout</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NVDA+n -> Preferences -> Browse mode</li>
      <li>Uncheck "Use screen layout when supported"</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Visual highlighting</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NVDA+n -> Preferences -> Vision</li>
      <li>Check "Enable highlighting"</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Save configuration</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NVDA+n</li>
      <li>Save configuration</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Navigate accessible website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Open Chrome</li>
      <li>Press alt+d to go to address bar</li>
      <li>Type www.nvaccess.org</li>
      <li>Press CTRL-key to pause speech</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Read the page</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>CTRL+home to go to top of page</li>
      <li>Press Arrow Down to discover each element</li>
      <li>You hear the text + its semantics</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Navigate faster</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Press NVDA+F7</li>
      <li>Provides by default a list of links</li>
      <li>Also possible to list headings, form controls etc.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Single letter navigation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>h for heading</li>
      <li>f for form control</li>
      <li>t for table</li>
      <li>Add shift to go back</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Browse mode and focus mode</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Filling in forms conflicts with single letter navigation</li>
      <li>For edit fields: switch to focus mode with Enter</li>
      <li>Back to browse mode with ESC</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Exercise</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Go to{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.anysurfer.be/en/">
          www.anysurfer.be/
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>Press e to go to edit field</li>
      <li>Press Enter to switch to focus mode</li>
      <li>Type screenreader</li>
      <li>Press ESC to leave focus mode</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Browse mode and focus mode</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When arrowing through a form, you have to manually activate focus mode
      </li>
      <li>
        When tabbing through a form, NVDA will switch to focus mode when needed
        and switch it back off when needed
      </li>
      <li>
        Take some time to{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://examples.anysurfer.be/4.1.1/labelsandformfields.html">
          practice
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
